@* =========================================================== 0 *@
<section class="section" id="how">
    <span class="section-tag">Before you start</span>
    <h2>0.1 How to use this workbook</h2>
    <p>
        Each scenario is a real piece of work you will do in your job, written as a short exercise. Do them
        <strong>in order</strong>: later scenarios use the leases, invoices and bills created by earlier ones,
        and the figures to expect assume you did.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Work in the practice company</strong>, never the live one. Check the company name at the top
            right of every screen before you start.</li>
        <li><strong>Menus are written as paths</strong>: <span class="path">Operations ▸ Customer Receipts</span> means
            open the <em>Operations</em> menu and choose <em>Customer Receipts</em>. Buttons are shown like
            <span class="btn">Save and Post</span>.</li>
        <li><strong>Dates.</strong> "<em>Day 1</em>" means the first day of the current month, "<em>Day 10</em>" the
            tenth, and "<em>month end</em>" its last day. Use the current year.</li>
        <li><strong>Each scenario ends with the result to expect</strong>, usually the journal entry. Open
            <span class="path">Operations ▸ Journal Inquiry</span> and compare. If your figures differ, find out why
            before moving on — that is where the learning is.</li>
        <li><strong>Two people</strong> are needed for the approval scenarios (T2 and T26): the trainee, and a trainer
            holding the approval permission. Nobody can approve their own work.</li>
        <li>The trainer signs each scenario off at the bottom of its box, and the record in Appendix B.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="watch">
        <strong>On a phone</strong>
        The workbook can be read on a phone, but enter the transactions on a computer: the forms have many fields.
        Wide tables scroll sideways inside their box.
    </div>

    <h2 id="cast" style="margin-top:1.4em">0.2 The practice company</h2>
    <p>Your trainer will have created these records. Ask for them if any is missing; setting them up is covered in the User Manual.</p>

    <h4>Properties and units</h4>
