    <h2 id="draft" style="margin-top:1.4em">0.3 Draft, Post and Journal Inquiry</h2>
    <p>
        Every transaction produces a journal entry. A <strong>draft</strong> journal is not in any report; a
        <strong>posted</strong> one is. Some screens post at once, others leave a draft you post yourself.
    </p>
    <div class="tbl"><table>
        <tr><th>Screens</th><th>What saving does</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Customer Invoices, Vendor Bills, Credit Notes</td><td>The <span class="btn">Post</span> button builds and posts the journal in one click.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Receipts, PDCs, Security Deposits, Vendor Payments, Petty Cash, Owner Withdrawals</td><td><span class="btn">Save and Post</span> posts at once. If it is refused, a yellow message says why and the entry stays a draft.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manual Journals, Revenue Recognition, Prepayments</td><td>Saving creates a draft. Post it from <span class="path">Operations ▸ Journal Inquiry</span>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fixed Assets</td><td>Posted immediately.</td></tr>
    </table></div>
    <div class="data">
        <strong>To post drafts</strong>
        <span class="path">Operations ▸ Journal Inquiry</span> → set <em>Posted Only</em> to <em>No</em> → <span class="btn">Go</span> →
        <span class="btn">Post</span> on one entry, or <span class="btn">Post All Drafts</span> for everything in the filter.
    </div>
</section>

@* =========================================================== 1 LEASING *@
<section class="section">
    <span class="section-tag">Module 1</span>
    <h2>Leasing</h2>
    <p class="intro">The lease drives everything else: when it takes effect it creates every rent invoice for its term and the month-by-month revenue plan.</p>

    <div class="scenario" id="t1">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T1</span><h3>Commercial lease, activated at once</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Leasing officer</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Master Data ▸ Leases</span><span><b>Time:</b> 10 min</span></div>
        <p>Al Noor Trading LLC signs a one-year lease of Office 301, paying quarterly.</p>
        <div class="data"><strong>Practice data</strong>
            Unit: Marina Heights – Office 301 · Tenant: Al Noor Trading LLC · Start: Day 1 · End: one year later, less one day ·
            Annual rent: 120,000 · Billing: Quarterly · Security deposit: 10,000
        </div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Open <span class="path">Master Data ▸ Leases</span> and select <span class="btn">Create Lease</span>.</li>
            <li>Choose the <em>Unit</em> and the <em>Tenant</em>.</li>
            <li>Enter the <em>Start Date</em>, <em>End Date</em> and <em>Annual Rent</em>.</li>
            <li>Set the <em>Billing Frequency</em> to <em>Quarterly</em>.</li>
            <li>Check the VAT treatment shown: it should be <em>Standard 5%</em> from the unit. Do not override it.</li>
            <li>Enter the <em>Security Deposit Amount</em> 10,000.</li>
            <li>Select <span class="btn">Save and Activate</span>. (If your company requires approval, use <span class="btn">Save and Submit for Approval</span> and ask the trainer to approve, as in T2.)</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            <ul>
                <li>The lease is <em>Active</em> with a generated contract code such as <code>…-U301-C001-2026</code>. The unit is <em>Occupied</em>.</li>
                <li><span class="path">Operations ▸ Customer Invoices</span> shows <strong>4 draft invoices</strong> of 30,000 + 1,500 VAT = <strong>31,500</strong>, dated Day 1 and every three months after.</li>
                <li><span class="path">System Setup ▸ Revenue Recognition</span> shows <strong>12 planned entries of 10,000</strong>, one at each month end.</li>
                <li>No journal yet: a lease is not a transaction.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t2">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T2</span><h3>Residential lease through approval</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Leasing officer + approver</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Master Data ▸ Leases, Master Data ▸ Approvals</span><span><b>Time:</b> 15 min</span></div>
        <p>Sara Ahmed rents Apartment 704. Contract approval is switched on, so a second person must approve. The approver first sends it back once.</p>
        <div class="data"><strong>Practice data</strong>
            Unit: Palm Residences – Apartment 704 · Tenant: Sara Ahmed · Start: Day 1 · One year · Annual rent: 72,000 · Billing: Quarterly ·
            Deposit: 5,000 (typed wrongly first as 50,000)
        </div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li><strong>Trainee:</strong> create the lease as in T1, but enter the deposit as 50,000, and select <span class="btn">Save and Submit for Approval</span>.</li>
            <li><strong>Approver:</strong> open <span class="path">Master Data ▸ Approvals</span>, open the request and read the terms and the invoices it will create.</li>
            <li><strong>Approver:</strong> select <em>Return to creator</em> with the reason "Deposit should be 5,000".</li>
            <li><strong>Trainee:</strong> the lease is back in <em>Draft</em>, marked <em>Returned</em> with the reason. Edit it, correct the deposit to 5,000, and select <span class="btn">Submit for approval</span>.</li>
            <li><strong>Approver:</strong> approve it.</li>
            <li><strong>Trainee:</strong> try to approve your own lease next time — the system refuses (four-eyes rule).</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            <ul>
                <li>The lease is <em>Active</em>. The history at the bottom shows the submission, the return with its reason, and the approval.</li>
                <li>4 draft invoices of <strong>18,000</strong> with <strong>no VAT</strong> (exempt residential), and 12 planned recognition entries of <strong>6,000</strong>.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Approver: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t3">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T3</span><h3>Managed property lease</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Leasing officer</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Master Data ▸ Leases</span><span><b>Time:</b> 10 min</span></div>
        <p>We manage Villa 12 for its landlord. The rent belongs to the landlord; only our 5% commission is our income.</p>
        <div class="data"><strong>Practice data</strong>
            Unit: Garden Villas – Villa 12 · Tenant: Omar Haddad · Start: Day 1 · One year · Annual rent: 90,000 · Billing: Semi-Annual · Deposit: none
        </div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Create and activate the lease as in T1.</li>
            <li>Open <span class="path">System Setup ▸ Revenue Recognition</span> and find the lease's entries.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            <ul>
                <li>2 draft invoices of <strong>45,000</strong> (no VAT), dated Day 1 and six months later.</li>
                <li>12 planned recognition entries of <strong>375</strong> each: 90,000 ÷ 12 × 5%. Only the commission becomes our revenue.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t4">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T4</span><h3>Print the contract and its QR label</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Leasing officer</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Master Data ▸ Leases</span><span><b>Time:</b> 5 min</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>On Al Noor's lease row, select <span class="btn">Draft Contract</span>. It opens in a new tab; print it or save it as PDF.</li>
            <li>Select <span class="btn">QR Label</span> and print the label for the contract file.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            A full tenancy agreement filled in from the lease (parties, premises, rent, payment schedule, deposit), and a label showing the contract code and a QR code.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>
</section>

@* =========================================================== 2 RECEIVABLES *@
<section class="section">
    <span class="section-tag">Module 2</span>
    <h2>Tenant receivables</h2>
    <p class="intro">Invoices are created by the lease; your job is to post them when due, correct them with credit notes, and record what the tenants pay.</p>

    <div class="scenario" id="t5">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T5</span><h3>Post and print a rent invoice</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Accountant</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Operations ▸ Customer Invoices</span><span><b>Time:</b> 10 min</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Open <span class="path">Operations ▸ Customer Invoices</span>.</li>
            <li>Find the <strong>Day 1</strong> invoice of each of the three leases (Al Noor 31,500 · Sara 18,000 · Omar 45,000).</li>
            <li>Select <span class="btn">Post</span> on each. The status becomes <em>Posted</em>.</li>
            <li>On Al Noor's invoice select <span class="btn">Tax Invoice</span>; on Sara's, <span class="btn">Invoice</span>. Compare the two documents.</li>
            <li>Leave the later invoices as drafts: they are posted when they fall due.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result — Al Noor (owned, standard rated)</strong>
            <div class="tbl"><table class="je">
                <tr><th>Account</th><th class="num">Debit</th><th class="num">Credit</th></tr>
                <tr><td>11200 Accounts Receivable</td><td class="num">31,500.00</td><td class="num"></td></tr>
                <tr><td>21200 Advances from Customers</td><td class="num"></td><td class="num">30,000.00</td></tr>
                <tr><td>21400 VAT Payable</td><td class="num"></td><td class="num">1,500.00</td></tr>
            </table></div>
            Sara's invoice has no VAT line. Omar's credits <strong>21500 Due to Landlords</strong> 45,000 instead of 21200, because the rent is the landlord's.
            Al Noor's is a <em>full tax invoice</em> showing both TRNs; Sara's is a plain <em>invoice</em> because exempt rent carries no VAT.
        </div>
        <div class="watch"><strong>Why no revenue?</strong>
            Billing is not earning. The invoice creates a receivable and unearned rent. Revenue arrives month by month through revenue recognition (T25).
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t6">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T6</span><h3>Credit note for a rent discount</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Accountant</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Operations ▸ Customer Invoices</span><span><b>Time:</b> 10 min</span></div>
        <p>Office 301 was handed over three days late; management agrees a discount of 1,000 plus VAT on the first invoice.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>On Al Noor's Day 1 invoice, select <span class="btn">Credit Note</span>.</li>
            <li><em>Credit note date</em>: Day 5. <em>Reason</em>: choose the discount reason from the list. <em>Explanation</em>: "Discount for late handover of Office 301".</li>
            <li><em>Net amount</em>: 1,000. VAT of 50 is calculated for you.</li>
            <li>Leave <em>Reverse into account</em> as it is, and select <span class="btn">Save &amp; Post</span>.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            <div class="tbl"><table class="je">
                <tr><th>Account</th><th class="num">Debit</th><th class="num">Credit</th></tr>
                <tr><td>21200 Advances from Customers</td><td class="num">1,000.00</td><td class="num"></td></tr>
                <tr><td>21400 VAT Payable</td><td class="num">50.00</td><td class="num"></td></tr>
                <tr><td>11200 Accounts Receivable</td><td class="num"></td><td class="num">1,050.00</td></tr>
            </table></div>
            The invoice now shows 1,050 credited and a balance of <strong>30,450</strong>.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t7">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T7</span><h3>Receipt by bank transfer</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Accountant</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Operations ▸ Customer Invoices / Customer Receipts</span><span><b>Time:</b> 5 min</span></div>
        <p>Al Noor transfers the balance of its first invoice.</p>
