<section class="section">
    <span class="section-tag">Module 3</span>
    <h2>Supplier payables</h2>
    <p class="intro">A bill records what you owe a supplier. VAT depends on whether the supplier is registered, and how much you can reclaim depends on what each line was for.</p>

    <div class="scenario" id="t13">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T13</span><h3>Bill from a VAT-registered supplier</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Accountant</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Operations ▸ Vendor Bills</span><span><b>Time:</b> 15 min</span></div>
        <p>Coastal Facility Services invoices this month's cleaning for two buildings on one document.</p>
        <div class="data"><strong>Practice data</strong>
            Supplier's bill no. CFS-5510 · Category: Building cleaning · Bill date and accounting date: Day 8 · Due: 30 days later
            <div class="tbl"><table>
                <tr><th>Line</th><th>Account</th><th>Property</th><th class="num">Qty × price</th><th>Taxable</th><th>Attribution</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Lobby and office cleaning</td><td>51100</td><td>Marina Heights</td><td class="num">1 × 4,000</td><td>Yes</td><td>Taxable</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Stairwell cleaning</td><td>51100</td><td>Palm Residences</td><td class="num">1 × 2,000</td><td>Yes</td><td>Exempt</td></tr>
            </table></div>
        </div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Select <span class="btn">New Bill</span> and choose the supplier. A blue banner says <em>Tax Invoice — 5% VAT applies</em>.</li>
            <li>Enter the supplier's bill number, category and dates.</li>
            <li>Enter the two lines as above; use <span class="btn">+ Add line</span> for the second. Watch the totals update.</li>
            <li>Select <span class="btn">Save Draft</span>, review, then <span class="btn">Post</span>.</li>
            <li>Select <span class="btn">Print</span> to see the bill document with the signature strip.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            <div class="tbl"><table class="je">
                <tr><th>Account</th><th class="num">Debit</th><th class="num">Credit</th></tr>
                <tr><td>51100 · Marina Heights</td><td class="num">4,000.00</td><td class="num"></td></tr>
                <tr><td>51100 · Palm Residences (2,000 + irrecoverable VAT 100)</td><td class="num">2,100.00</td><td class="num"></td></tr>
                <tr><td>11300 VAT Recoverable</td><td class="num">200.00</td><td class="num"></td></tr>
                <tr><td>21100 Accounts Payable</td><td class="num"></td><td class="num">6,300.00</td></tr>
            </table></div>
            VAT on the residential line cannot be reclaimed, so it is added to that line's cost. Your own bill number (BILL-…) is issued on saving.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t14">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T14</span><h3>Bill from an unregistered supplier</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Accountant</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Operations ▸ Vendor Bills</span><span><b>Time:</b> 5 min</span></div>
        <div class="data"><strong>Practice data</strong>
