@* =========================================================== 6 CLOSING *@
<section class="section">
    <span class="section-tag">Module 6</span>
    <h2>Month-end and year-end</h2>
    <p class="intro">The Closing Cockpit checks that every recurring process reached the general ledger before a month is locked. Once closed, nothing can be posted, reset or changed in that month.</p>

    <div class="scenario" id="t25">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T25</span><h3>Close the month in the Closing Cockpit</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Accountant / finance supervisor</span><span><b>Menu:</b> System Setup ▸ Closing Cockpit</span><span><b>Time:</b> 20 min</span></div>
        <p>In training, close the month you have been working in. Your trainer may first move the practice dates so that the month has ended.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Open the cockpit. Select the month's tile. Read every line of its checklist and its light:
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Green</strong> — processed and the ledger agrees.</li>
                    <li><strong>Amber</strong> — review; does not stop the close once you tick that you reviewed it.</li>
                    <li><strong>Red</strong> — not processed; blocks the close.</li>
                    <li><strong>Grey</strong> — nothing to do this month.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li><em>Revenue recognition</em> is red: select <span class="btn">Run recognition</span>. It turns green with <strong>16,375</strong> recognised (10,000 + 6,000 + 375).</li>
            <li><em>Depreciation</em> is red (the generator): select <span class="btn">Run depreciation</span>. Green at <strong>525</strong>.</li>
            <li><em>Prepayment amortisation</em> is red (insurance): select <span class="btn">Run amortisation</span>. Green at <strong>1,000</strong>.</li>
            <li><em>No draft journals</em>: if red, read which drafts are listed. Post genuine ones with <span class="btn">Post all drafts</span>; delete or correct any that should not exist.</li>
            <li>Read the amber lines (for example cheques due but not cleared). Decide whether each is acceptable.</li>
            <li>Now do T23 (commission invoices), then return here.</li>
            <li>When nothing is red, tick <em>I have reviewed the amber warnings</em> and select <span class="btn">Close</span>.</li>
            <li>Try to post anything dated in that month — a receipt, a journal, a reset. Every attempt is refused.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            The tile shows a padlock. The period history records who closed it, when, and the warnings acknowledged. The dashboard's
            <em>Unclosed Periods</em> section no longer lists the month.
        </div>
        <div class="tbl"><table class="je">
            <tr><th>Month-end entry</th><th>Debit</th><th>Credit</th><th class="num">Amount</th></tr>
            <tr><td>Revenue – Al Noor</td><td>21200 Advances from Customers</td><td>41100 Rental Revenue – Owned</td><td class="num">10,000.00</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Revenue – Sara</td><td>21200 Advances from Customers</td><td>41100 Rental Revenue – Owned</td><td class="num">6,000.00</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Commission – Villa 12</td><td>21500 Due to Landlords</td><td>42100 Management Fee Revenue</td><td class="num">375.00</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Depreciation – generator</td><td>62100 Depreciation Expense</td><td>15300 Accumulated Depreciation</td><td class="num">525.00</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Insurance – month 1</td><td>51100 Property Operating Expenses</td><td>11500 Prepaid Expenses</td><td class="num">1,000.00</td></tr>
        </table></div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t26">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T26</span><h3>Reopen a closed month on request</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Accountant + approver</span><span><b>Menu:</b> System Setup ▸ Closing Cockpit / Period Reopen Requests</span><span><b>Time:</b> 15 min</span></div>
        <p>After closing, a supplier's bill for the month turns up that must be in it.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li><strong>Trainee:</strong> select the closed month's tile. Under <em>Ask for this period to be reopened</em>, write a real reason (at least 15 characters), e.g. "Coastal bill CFS-5530 for this month's pest control arrived after closing", and select <span class="btn">Request reopening</span>.</li>
            <li><strong>Approver:</strong> open <span class="path">System Setup ▸ Period Reopen Requests</span> (the red badge shows how many wait). Read the reason.</li>
            <li><strong>Approver:</strong> first try <span class="btn">Turn down</span> without a comment — a comment is required. Then add the comment "Approved – post the bill and close again today" and select <span class="btn">Approve &amp; reopen</span>.</li>
            <li><strong>Trainee:</strong> the month shows <em>Reopened</em>. Enter and post the bill (500 + VAT, Marina Heights, taxable).</li>
            <li><strong>Trainee:</strong> close the month again through the checklist, as in T25.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            The request shows <em>Reclosed</em>. The period history lists: Closed → Reopen requested → Reopened (with reason and approver) → Closed again.
            The requester could not approve their own request.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Approver: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t27">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T27</span><h3>VAT return and VAT payment</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Accountant</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Reporting ▸ VAT Return, Operations ▸ Manual Journals</span><span><b>Time:</b> 15 min</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Open <span class="path">Reporting ▸ VAT Return</span> for the current quarter and select <span class="btn">Refresh</span>.</li>
            <li>Find each of your documents: Al Noor's invoice (standard), the credit note (<em>Less credit notes</em>), Sara's and Omar's invoices (exempt), the commission invoice (<em>management commission to landlords</em>), and the bills by attribution.</li>
            <li>Note <em>Output Tax Due</em>, <em>Input Tax Recoverable</em> and <em>Net VAT payable</em>.</li>
            <li>Record the payment to the FTA with a manual journal: Dr 21400 VAT Payable (output tax) · Cr 11300 VAT Recoverable (input tax) · Cr 11100 Cash (the net amount). Post it.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            With only this workbook's documents, output tax is 1,500 − 50 + 18.75 = <strong>1,468.75</strong>; recoverable input tax is the 5% on the taxable bill lines.
            After the payment journal, 21400 and 11300 are back to zero for the quarter.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t28">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T28</span><h3>Check the reports</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Accountant / supervisor</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Reporting</span><span><b>Time:</b> 20 min</span></div>
        <p>Open each report for the month you closed and answer the question beside it.</p>
        <div class="tbl"><table>
            <tr><th>Report</th><th>Question to answer</th></tr>
            <tr><td>Trial Balance</td><td>Do total debits equal total credits?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Profit &amp; Loss</td><td>Is rental revenue 16,000 and management fee revenue 375? Where are depreciation and insurance?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Balance Sheet</td><td>What does 21200 Advances from Customers hold, and why? What is in 21300?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Tenant Statement — Al Noor</td><td>Invoice 31,500, credit 1,050, receipt 30,450: is the balance nil?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Vendor Statement — Coastal</td><td>Which bills are still unpaid?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>P&amp;L by Property</td><td>Which building carries the generator depreciation and the cleaning?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>General Ledger — 11100</td><td>Can you find every receipt and payment from this workbook?</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Owner Withdrawals</td><td>Is the 5,000 under Education?</td></tr>
        </table></div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t29">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T29</span><h3>Year-end close</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Finance supervisor (trainer demonstrates)</span><span><b>Menu:</b> System Setup ▸ Closing Cockpit</span><span><b>Time:</b> 15 min</span></div>
        <p>Done once a year, after all twelve months are closed. The trainer demonstrates it on a practice year.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Choose the fiscal year in the cockpit. Under <em>Year-end close</em>, read any red lines: every period closed, the previous year closed, the retained earnings account mapped.</li>
            <li>Review the preview: revenue to clear, expenses to clear, and the net profit or loss going to retained earnings.</li>
            <li>Select <span class="btn">Close fiscal year</span> and confirm.</li>
            <li>Open <em>Opening balances carried into</em> the next year and check that debits equal credits.</li>
            <li>Run the Profit &amp; Loss for the closed year: it still shows the year's result. Run the Balance Sheet one day into the new year: the result now sits in 32100 Retained Earnings.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            One posted closing entry on the last day of the year: every revenue account debited, every expense account credited, and the difference to 32100 Retained Earnings.
            Balance sheet accounts carry into the new year unchanged. If any month of that year is later reopened, the year close is undone and must be run again.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Seen</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>
</section>

