        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            The material posted Dr 21500 Due to Landlords · Cr 11650 120, tagged to Garden Villas. The statement lists it under "maintenance and expenses charged to the owner" and the owner's share is 120 lower. The profitability report shows Garden Villas' rent, our 5% commission, its VAT, the 120 of costs, the owner's net income and margin — and our commission as the company's income.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t37">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T37</span><h3>Keep a tenant's Emirates ID and passport</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Master data owner</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Master Data ▸ Tenants · Master Data ▸ Document Expiry</span><span><b>Time:</b> 15 min</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Open Sara Ahmed in edit and go to <strong>Tenant documents</strong> at the bottom.</li>
            <li>Upload a scan or photo of an Emirates ID (your trainer provides a sample): type Emirates ID, leave number and dates empty, keep <strong>Read the Emirates ID / passport</strong> ticked, <span class="btn">Upload</span>.</li>
            <li>Read the message, then look at the EID expiry field on the form.</li>
            <li>Upload a passport with reading switched off: number P1234567, expiry a date last month.</li>
            <li>Open <span class="path">Master Data ▸ Document Expiry</span>.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            The ID number (if Sara had none), the expiry date and nationality were filled in; a different number already on file is reported, not overwritten. The passport expiry shows in red as expired on the form, and Sara's passport heads the Document Expiry list as expired.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t38">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T38</span><h3>Attach the attested contract</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Leasing officer</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Master Data ▸ Leases</span><span><b>Time:</b> 5 min</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Open the contract from T1. Under <strong>Contract documents</strong> it says no attested contract is on file.</li>
            <li>Upload the PDF of the contract attested by the municipality: type "Attested contract (Municipality)", number RAK-ATT-T38.</li>
            <li>Open Document Expiry again.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            The warning is gone and the count of running contracts without an attested copy is one lower.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t39">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T39</span><h3>Read a scanned supplier invoice</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Accountant</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Operations ▸ Vendor Bills ▸ New</span><span><b>Time:</b> 10 min</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>On <span class="btn">New Vendor Bill</span>, use <strong>Read a scanned invoice</strong> with a supplier invoice from Coastal Facility Services (your trainer provides the PDF). <span class="btn">Read invoice</span>.</li>
            <li>Compare every field with the document: supplier, their number, dates, each line's description, quantity and unit price, VAT, and the figures in the blue panel.</li>
            <li>Choose any missing account, <span class="btn">Save Draft</span>, then post it.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            The bill's totals equal the invoice's. Warnings explain anything that differs (a discount line, an unknown supplier). Nothing is saved until you save.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scenario" id="t40">
        <div class="scenario-head"><span class="id">T40</span><h3>Let the AI Assistant do the typing (optional)</h3></div>
        <div class="facts"><span><b>Role:</b> Any user with the assistant</span><span><b>Menu:</b> Assistant button</span><span><b>Time:</b> 15 min</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Open the assistant: "Record a petty cash voucher of 150 for cleaning materials, paid to Al Noor Supermarket, receipt R-5531, property Marina Heights." Check the card and <span class="btn">Confirm</span>.</li>
            <li>Open a New Vendor Bill, then ask: "Fill this in for Coastal Facility Services, invoice CFS-9, 12 AC filters at 150." Check the yellow fields and save it yourself.</li>
            <li>Select the paperclip and attach the invoice from T39: the assistant repeats what it read.</li>
            <li>Ask: "Open a new unit for Marina Heights, 7th floor, 1,250 sq ft, rent 82,000."</li>
            <li>Ask: "What is the market rent for a 2-bedroom apartment in Al Marjan Island?"</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="expect"><strong>Expected result</strong>
            Only a click on Confirm or on the screen's Save button saves anything. The market rent answer gives sources with dates beside your own rents for the same kind of unit.
        </div>
        <div class="signoff"><span><i class="box"></i>Done</span><span>Trainee: ____________</span><span>Trainer: ____________</span><span>Date: ________</span></div>
    </div>
</section>

@* =========================================================== APPENDICES *@
<section class="section" id="a1">
    <span class="section-tag">Appendix A</span>
    <h2>Messages you may see, and what to do</h2>
    <div class="tbl"><table>
        <tr><th>Message or situation</th><th>Meaning</th><th>What to do</th></tr>
        <tr><td>"… is closed. … cannot be created, posted, changed or removed in a closed period."</td><td>The date falls in a closed month.</td><td>Date it in an open month, or ask for the month to be reopened (T26).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"Invoice … has not been posted yet"</td><td>You are receiving money or clearing a cheque against a draft invoice.</td><td>Post the invoice first (T5).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"Bill … has not been posted yet"</td><td>You are paying a draft bill.</td><td>Post the bill first.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"Journal entry is not balanced"</td><td>Debits and credits differ, or a line has both.</td><td>Check each line's figures.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"This voucher would take the float below zero"</td><td>Not enough cash in the petty cash float.</td><td>Replenish the float first.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"The unit is already taken for these dates by contract …"</td><td>Another active or waiting lease covers the dates.</td><td>Check the dates, or end the other lease.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"The most that can be paid to … is …"</td><td>The landlord payment exceeds the balance.</td><td>Pay no more than the balance shown.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>I saved it but it is not in the Trial Balance</td><td>It is a draft.</td><td>Post it from Journal Inquiry (0.3).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Reset to Draft is refused</td><td>Something depends on it (a receipt, a payment, a cleared cheque) or the month is closed.</td><td>Reset the later item first, or post a correcting journal.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"Maintenance requests are on hold for your account…"</td><td>The tenant has an overdue invoice or a returned cheque not replaced.</td><td>Collect the money or the replacement cheque; the hold lifts by itself (T33).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"No user carries out maintenance jobs yet"</td><td>Nobody has the Maintenance Engineer role, so jobs wait unassigned.</td><td>Create the maintenance user (T32); assign waiting jobs from the job card.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"Give the bill or receipt number the item was bought on"</td><td>A material bought for a job needs its bill or receipt.</td><td>Enter the bill or petty cash receipt number.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"No vendor matched … Select the supplier, or create it first"</td><td>The scanned invoice's supplier is not in Vendors.</td><td>Choose the supplier, or create the vendor and read the invoice again.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"Check: the document reads …, but the tenant record has …"</td><td>The Emirates ID or passport number on the scan differs from the tenant's.</td><td>Check which is right and correct the tenant if needed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>A red light in the Closing Cockpit</td><td>A process for the month has not reached the ledger.</td><td>Use the line's Run button or open the screen named beside it.</td></tr>
    </table></div>
</section>

